Your project targets **net10.0**, so the best approach for `File.*` and `Directory.*` is the established **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — no need to write custom wrappers.

## Recommended: Adopt `System.IO.Abstractions`

### 1. Install the packages

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions                      # production code
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers  # tests
```

### 2. Register in DI (Program.cs / Startup.cs)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

Looking at your `ReportGenerator`, you'd refactor it like this:

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {DateTime.UtcNow:O}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
Assert.Contains("sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
```

## Bonus: Other statics in `ReportGenerator`

Your class also uses `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.*`:

| Static | Recommended abstraction |
|--------|------------------------|
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | **`TimeProvider`** (built-in in .NET 10) — inject `TimeProvider`, call `timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`, test with `FakeTimeProvider` from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` |
| `Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable` | Custom `IEnvironmentProvider` with one method, or pass config values directly |
| `Console.WriteLine` | `ILogger<T>` (already built-in) — preferred over wrapping Console |

The filesystem statics (`File.*`, `Directory.*`, `Path.*`) are the most impactful to wrap first since they make tests slow, flaky, and environment-dependent. `System.IO.Abstractions` handles all three in one package.
